WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.760
Internal network abuse matters because healthcare applications often handle ePHI,

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.380
user identity, clinical workflows, patient portals, APIs, and integrations.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.600
Teams should look for this issue in user-facing features, administrative tools,

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:17.100
background jobs, and service-to-service communication.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.280
Cloud metadata exploitation matters because healthcare applications often handle ePHI,

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.780
user identity, clinical workflows, patient portals, APIs, and integrations.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.920
Teams should look for this issue in user-facing features, administrative tools,

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.420
background jobs, and service-to-service communication.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.680
Trust boundary violations matters because healthcare applications often handle ePHI,

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:46.580
user identity, clinical workflows, patient portals, APIs, and integrations.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:51.200
Teams should look for this issue in user-facing features, administrative tools,

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.460
background jobs, and service-to-service communication.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:01:00.120
Network segmentation, URL allowlists, and egress filtering help reduce SSRF risk.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:07.540
Selected HIPAA mappings for this topic include Section 164.312(a)(1) - Access control;

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:13.840
Section 164.312(e)(1) - Transmission security;

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:20.460
Section 164.308(a)(1)(ii)(B) - Risk management.
